------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fonts
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The synthetic plate renderer does NOT bundle a licence-plate font. This is
deliberate: the freely-circulating digitisations of the German FE-Schrift (the
official "fälschungserschwerende Schrift" defined in Anlage 4 of the
Fahrzeug-Zulassungsverordnung) have unclear or non-permissive redistribution
terms, which conflicts with this project's clean-provenance stance. Because this
is a *detector* (it learns only *where* a plate is, not how to read it), exact
glyph fidelity does not affect the result.

At runtime the renderer resolves a font in this order (see
src/plate_redactor/generator/fonts.py):

  1. an explicit path passed via `--font`
  2. the PLATE_REDACTOR_FONT environment variable
  3. any .ttf/.otf placed in src/plate_redactor/generator/assets/fonts/
     (git-ignored; this is where you may drop a real FE-Schrift you are
     licensed to use)
  4. a commonly-installed system font (DejaVu / Liberation / Arial / Helvetica),
     used at runtime only and never redistributed by this project
  5. Pillow's built-in scalable default font (permissively licensed; ships with
     the Pillow dependency) as a guaranteed fallback

If you add an FE-Schrift or other plate font under assets/fonts/, record its
source and licence here, and confirm you are permitted to use (and, if you
publish the dataset, redistribute) it.
